{%- doc -%}
  Pill-style category filter for the Shop All collection — the design's
  All / Tea / Sauces & Chutneys / Pantry & Gifts row, with a right-aligned
  product count. Not a fork of blocks/filters.liquid (1476 lines, handles
  price/boolean/swatch filters and a vertical drawer variant this page
  doesn't use) — this covers only the one horizontal, tag-based case the
  design needs, reusing Horizon's real facets-form-component /
  facet-inputs-component / facet-clear-component JS (assets/facets.js) so
  filtering stays genuine AJAX, in place, no page reload — the same
  mechanism the native filters block uses, not a reimplementation of it.

  Inserted via an explicit `content_for 'block'` call in
  sections/main-collection.liquid (that section has no open/merchant-
  addable block slot — filters and _product-card are both fixed, hardcoded
  calls, confirmed by reading the file directly rather than assumed) — see
  ARCHITECTURE.md for that one-line core-file edit, signed off before
  writing, and the native filters block's own visibility handled by this
  block's own stylesheet below (see the CSS comment for why).

  Labels are merchant-editable settings, not the raw tag string — a tag
  value ("condiments") and its design label ("Sauces & Chutneys") are
  unrelated strings on purpose, per instruction, so wording can change
  without touching tags in Admin. Matching is case-insensitive on both
  sides (the tag's actual stored casing isn't guaranteed to match what the
  collection's automation condition displays) — downcase before comparing,
  never assume exact casing.

  Section-level insertion means every collection page using main-
  collection.liquid gets this block, not just Shop All — so it only
  renders when the underlying tag filter actually has 2+ of the three
  known values present. On Tea/Condiments/Pantry, every product shares
  exactly one of the three tags, so the count never reaches 2 and this
  renders nothing; the native filters block (hidden only inside the
  conditional below, see the {% style %} block) is left visible there
  instead, since there's nothing of ours to show in its place. Self-
  managing by design, not a per-page check — if the client ever creates
  another multi-category collection sharing this section, the row appears
  there too without a code change. See ARCHITECTURE.md.
{%- enddoc -%}

{% liquid
  assign block_settings = block.settings
  assign products_count = collection.products_count

  assign tag_filter = nil
  assign known_tag_value_count = 0
  for f in collection.filters
    if f.type == 'list'
      assign match_count_this_filter = 0
      for v in f.values
        assign downcased_v = v.value | downcase
        if downcased_v == 'tea' or downcased_v == 'condiments' or downcased_v == 'pantry'
          assign match_count_this_filter = match_count_this_filter | plus: 1
        endif
      endfor
      if match_count_this_filter > known_tag_value_count
        assign tag_filter = f
        assign known_tag_value_count = match_count_this_filter
      endif
    endif
  endfor
%}
{% if known_tag_value_count >= 2 %}
  {% liquid
    assign has_active_tag = false
    if tag_filter and tag_filter.active_values.size > 0
      assign has_active_tag = true
    endif

    assign lambruk_tag_param_name = 'filter.p.tag'
    if tag_filter and tag_filter.values.first
      assign lambruk_tag_param_name = tag_filter.values.first.param_name
    endif

    assign page_type_attribute = 'data-page-type="collection"'
    assign collection_id_attribute = 'data-collection-id="' | append: collection.id | append: '"'
    assign collection_handle_attribute = 'data-collection-handle="' | append: collection.handle | append: '"'
    assign results_count_attribute = 'data-results-count="' | append: products_count | append: '"'
  %}

<script src="{{ 'facets.js' | asset_url }}" type="module" fetchpriority="low"></script>

<div
  class="lambruk-tag-filter spacing-style"
  style="
    grid-column: var(--grid-column--desktop);
    --grid-column--desktop: var(--centered);
    --grid-column--mobile: var(--centered);
  "
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <facets-form-component
    class="lambruk-tag-filter__form-wrapper"
    section-id="{{ section.id }}"
    form-style="horizontal"
    {{ collection_id_attribute }}
    {{ collection_handle_attribute }}
    {{ page_type_attribute }}
    {{ results_count_attribute }}
  >
    <form
      action="{{ collection.url }}"
      id="LambrukTagFilterForm-{{ block.id }}"
      class="lambruk-tag-filter__form"
      ref="facetsForm"
    >
      <div class="lambruk-tag-filter__row">
        <facet-inputs-component
          on:change="/updateFilters"
          id="lambruk-tag-filter-inputs-{{ block.id }}"
          class="lambruk-tag-filter__pills"
        >
          {%- comment -%}
            "All" was originally a facet-clear-component (Horizon's own
            "clear this filter group" button). Reverted: its clearFilter()
            (assets/facets.js) only calls facetsForm.updateFilters() after
            finding an ancestor <details> containing a
            <facet-status-component> — a dependency on list-filter.liquid's
            own accordion wrapper, undocumented, found by reading the
            source after "All" visually cleared the checked pills live but
            never actually re-filtered (URL and product count both stayed
            on the previous tag). Tried satisfying it with an inert
            `<details open>` + hidden status component; `display: contents`
            doesn't fully dissolve `<details>` in practice — its own
            box/marker persisted and broke the row layout, confirmed live,
            not assumed from how the property is supposed to work.

            "All" is a radio instead, in the same input group as the three
            tag values, empty value. Same on:change path as the other
            three (FacetInputsComponent.updateFilters(), no details
            dependency at all) — verified live before committing to this:
            an empty filter.p.tag value clears the active filter rather
            than matching zero products, confirmed by the count returning
            to 52 and the product grid returning to the full unfiltered
            set, not just the empty param being silently dropped.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="lambruk-tag-filter__pill-wrapper">
            <input
              type="radio"
              name="{{ lambruk_tag_param_name }}"
              id="LambrukFilter-{{ block.id }}-all"
              value=""
              class="lambruk-tag-filter__input"
              {% unless has_active_tag %}
                checked
              {% endunless %}
              ref="facetInputs[]"
            >
            <label
              class="lambruk-tag-filter__pill lambruk-tag-filter__pill-label"
              for="LambrukFilter-{{ block.id }}-all"
            >
              {{ block_settings.all_label }}
            </label>
          </div>

          {% if tag_filter %}
            {%- comment -%}
              Design order is All / Tea / Sauces & Chutneys / Pantry & Gifts.
              tag_filter.values comes back from Shopify's own facet API in
              its own order (alphabetical by tag value: condiments, pantry,
              tea), which put Tea last — confirmed live, not assumed.
              Iterating a fixed key order here instead, looking up the
              matching facet value for each, rather than trusting the
              API's order.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {% liquid
              assign ordered_tag_keys = 'tea,condiments,pantry' | split: ','
              assign pill_index = 0
            %}
            {% for tag_key in ordered_tag_keys %}
              {% for value in tag_filter.values %}
                {% liquid
                  assign downcased_value = value.value | downcase
                  assign display_label = value.label
                  assign matches_current_key = false
                  if downcased_value == tag_key
                    assign matches_current_key = true
                    case tag_key
                      when 'tea'
                        assign display_label = block_settings.tea_label
                      when 'condiments'
                        assign display_label = block_settings.condiments_label
                      when 'pantry'
                        assign display_label = block_settings.pantry_label
                    endcase
                  endif
                %}
                {% if matches_current_key %}
                  {% assign pill_index = pill_index | plus: 1 %}
                  <div class="lambruk-tag-filter__pill-wrapper">
                    <input
                      type="radio"
                      name="{{ value.param_name }}"
                      id="LambrukFilter-{{ block.id }}-{{ pill_index }}"
                      value="{{ value.value }}"
                      class="lambruk-tag-filter__input"
                      {% if value.active %}
                        checked
                      {% endif %}
                      ref="facetInputs[]"
                    >
                    <label
                      class="lambruk-tag-filter__pill lambruk-tag-filter__pill-label"
                      for="LambrukFilter-{{ block.id }}-{{ pill_index }}"
                    >
                      {{ display_label }}
                    </label>
                  </div>
                {% endif %}
              {% endfor %}
            {% endfor %}
          {% endif %}
        </facet-inputs-component>

        <span class="lambruk-tag-filter__count">
          {{- 'content.item_count' | t: count: products_count -}}
        </span>
      </div>
    </form>
  </facets-form-component>
</div>

{% style %}
  /* Hides the native `filters` block's own rendering (sort dropdown, grid-
     density toggle, and its own tag checkboxes) for this section instance
     only — scoped to #shopify-section-{{ section.id }}, not a blanket rule.
     Lives inside the known_tag_value_count >= 2 conditional above on
     purpose: on Tea/Condiments/Pantry, this pill row doesn't render at all
     (only one known tag each), so this rule doesn't either — the native
     filters block is left visible there instead of being hidden with
     nothing in its place. Deliberate, not a removal: enable_sorting/
     enable_grid_density stay "true" in collection.all.json's own filters
     block settings, so both controls are still fully configured and
     reachable again by deleting this one rule — no rebuild. See
     ARCHITECTURE.md. The stylesheet tag can't hold this — it rejects any
     Liquid variable (theme check's StaticStylesheetAndJavascriptTags,
     confirmed live, not assumed) since it's static/shared across every
     instance of this block; this style tag is Shopify's per-render
     alternative and does allow section.id here. */
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .facets-block-wrapper--horizontal {
    display: none;
  }
{% endstyle %}
{% endif %}

{% stylesheet %}
  .lambruk-tag-filter__row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 28px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #E3D6C5;
  }

  /* Design source: filter row's own border-bottom (above) plus a separate
     40px margin-top on the product grid that follows it — two distinct
     gaps, not one shared value. Confirmed live before this fix: the grid
     sat with 0px between it and the divider, not just "tighter than
     design" — the .collection-wrapper grid's own gap doesn't reach here.

     Not a sibling selector: confirmed live that .product-grid isn't a
     direct (or even general) sibling of .lambruk-tag-filter at all — it's
     nested two levels deeper inside an unnamed wrapper div inside
     .collection-wrapper. :has() instead, scoped to "the collection-wrapper
     that contains this block" rather than depending on exact sibling
     structure, which is also more robust against Horizon changing that
     intermediate markup later. Scoped for free either way: this block
     only renders at all when 2+ of the three known tags are present (see
     doc comment at top), i.e. Shop All only — Tea/Condiments/Pantry never
     render .lambruk-tag-filter, so this rule can't reach them. */
  .collection-wrapper:has(.lambruk-tag-filter) .product-grid {
    margin-top: 40px;
  }

  .lambruk-tag-filter__pills {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .lambruk-tag-filter__pill-wrapper {
    position: relative;
  }

  .lambruk-tag-filter__input {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    opacity: 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    appearance: none;
  }

  .lambruk-tag-filter__pill {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 9px 18px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid #E3D6C5;
    background: transparent;
    color: #131A3E;
    font-family: var(--font-body--family);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: normal;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background-color 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease, border-color 0.15s ease;
  }

  .lambruk-tag-filter__input:checked + .lambruk-tag-filter__pill,
  .lambruk-tag-filter__pill--active {
    border-color: #131A3E;
    background: #131A3E;
    color: #F7F5F2;
  }

  .lambruk-tag-filter__input:focus-visible + .lambruk-tag-filter__pill {
    outline: 2px solid #131A3E;
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .lambruk-tag-filter__count {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: #4A5478;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:names.lambruk_tag_filter",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:content.lambruk_tag_filter_labels"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "all_label",
      "label": "t:settings.lambruk_tag_filter_all_label",
      "default": "All"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "tea_label",
      "label": "t:settings.lambruk_tag_filter_tea_label",
      "default": "Tea"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "condiments_label",
      "label": "t:settings.lambruk_tag_filter_condiments_label",
      "default": "Sauces & Chutneys"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "pantry_label",
      "label": "t:settings.lambruk_tag_filter_pantry_label",
      "default": "Pantry & Gifts"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
